Z||000016||StuGood||10-26-2001||05:46 PM||||I think I read somewhere that one could straighten the (old) aluminum pedal assembly with a big pair of pliers, and make it work again.  For those of you needing a driveable car post haste, that could be a temporary solution.<P>It's not like the pedal asm. breaks, it just bends.  And it doesn't just fail instantly, anyway - my 1986 V6 SE 4-speed had an aluminum pedal that worked fine for years.       <P>Maybe that'll give Rodney time to come up with an aftermarket pedal  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"> ||||reg||3
